# Owner Identity Derivation — Full Map

All derivation logic lives in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/` (small standalone helper classes + AspectJ aspects), is assembled into the response by the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`, and the response shape is defined in the OpenAPI spec `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (the `OwnerDto` is generated from it — there is no hand-written `OwnerDto.java`).

Important up front: the code, the OpenAPI descriptions, and the test reference tables **disagree** on how "region/locality" is derived (postcode-band vs. city-lookup) and how `identityKey`/`timezone` are built. Details flagged inline below — you will want to reconcile these when modifying.

---

## 1. The identifier derivation algorithms (verbatim)

### region code — `OwnerMemberId.region()`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerMemberId.java`

```java
39	    /** Postcode band (4-digit / 100) -> region code. */
40	    private static final Map<Integer, String> REGION = Map.of(20, "NSW", 30, "VIC", 40, "QLD");
41
42	    /** The region code derived from the owner's postcode band, or "UNKNOWN". */
43	    public static String region(Owner owner) {
44	        String pc = owner.getPostcode();
45	        int band = pc != null && pc.matches("[0-9]{4}") ? Integer.parseInt(pc) / 100 : -1;
46	        return REGION.getOrDefault(band, "UNKNOWN");
47	    }
```
This is the single region source. It is reused by `OwnerSegment`, and the mapper feeds it into the response `locality` field. Note: region is derived from **postcode**, not city — contradicting the OpenAPI `locality` description and the test `CITY_REGION` table (both say Sydney->NSW etc.).

### memberId — `OwnerMemberId.base()` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`)
Same file:
```java
49	    /** The base memberId before any collision suffix, or {@code null} when the date is absent. */
50	    public static String base(Owner owner) {
51	        LocalDate registered = owner.getRegistrationDate();
52	        if (registered == null) {
53	            return null;
54	        }
55	        String body = region(owner) + String.format("%02d", OwnerFiscalYear.yearOf(registered) % 100) + hash8(owner);
56	        return body + OwnerCheckDigit.luhn(body);
57	    }
58
59	    private static String hash8(Owner owner) {
60	        try {
61	            byte[] d = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
62	                .digest((owner.getTelephone() + owner.getLastName()).getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
63	            return String.format("%02X%02X%02X%02X", d[0], d[1], d[2], d[3]);
64	        }
```
So `region` is mixed into `memberId` as its leading segment. FY comes from `OwnerFiscalYear.yearOf` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../advice/OwnerFiscalYear.java`, fiscal year starts 1 July), check digit from `OwnerCheckDigit.luhn` (`.../OwnerCheckDigit.java`).

The `memberId` is assigned onto the owner's `customerCode` field before save, then deduplicated:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice.java`
